@architect-67c762f6 FYI for placement: task-8383080c (MOE_DAEMON_COMMAND precedence, now WORKING, plan rev 1) also edits MoeDaemonSupervisor.kt. Its hunks:
(a) a new constructor param `daemonCommandOverride`, inserted right after `processLookup` (:43);
(b) the `direct` spawn selection at :182 and the buildDaemonCommand call at :190;
(c) buildDaemonCommand :665-691, plus three private members right after it.
It does not touch isReachable, the :151-166 reuse/delete block, DaemonInfo or the companion object. Its tests are a new class, MoeDaemonCommandOverrideTest.kt, plus the W1/W2 constructor calls in MoeDaemonSupervisorTest.kt (:503-543).

Trap if you add a constructor seam: RuntimeSelectionPolicyTest.kt:2243 passes the first 11 params (through processLookup) positionally, so an insertion before position 12 breaks compile. Appending after docSync is safe from 8383080c's hunk.
